{"id": "EUVD-2026-80601", "enisaUuid": "d790ce1b-aff5-3b4c-82d3-d746d313e823", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: dw-edma: Initialize IRQ data before requesting IRQs\n\ndw_edma_irq_request() passes struct dw_edma_irq to request_irq() before\ndw_edma_channel_setup() fills the back pointer. A shared interrupt can\ntherefore enter the handler with dw_irq->dw still NULL, leading to a\nNULL pointer dereference.\n\nSet the back pointer before installing each handler.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:56:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b86280b12ccf33b68b309b7cb0e4476894dfe77c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/07e50cef557def076418c67051a336e4c6bd50e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/17ef63843c0fcbf1efdfbbfb0f5584a5ea2c91ba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d232bc6cf4562132ef50644484dfd4b23a593295", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fac202d73e7a649b7d4010325c6c6dcd9334fe65", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d91fb6c0d10dad32929dc5c6850f89df34e1bfcd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/647217abea849d3d45f8cb0b8ee5b78d50f26985"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89993", "GHSA-36xx-949x-639g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0aae31b7-26e1-373b-8b4c-0c981fe92951", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e63d79d1ffcd2201a2dbff1d7a1184b8f3ec74cf <17ef63843c0fcbf1efdfbbfb0f5584a5ea2c91ba"}, {"id": "0e1f6980-b838-31e5-aa91-3de1cfd29d14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "3663479a-7f05-30d2-8456-f962fe930e21", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6b4bc363-321e-37fc-aac1-1c2737e70eb2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e63d79d1ffcd2201a2dbff1d7a1184b8f3ec74cf <b86280b12ccf33b68b309b7cb0e4476894dfe77c"}, {"id": "